<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  M1K3iOS.entitlements — the iPhone/iPad target's entitlements.

  iOS needs none of the Mac's set: the sandbox is implicit, files arrive through
  the document picker, networking has no entitlement (local-network + Bonjour are
  Info.plist usage keys), and the mic/calendar/location are usage strings + TCC.

  The one entry is Increased Memory Limit. iOS jetsams a foreground app at a
  FRACTION of physical RAM; the mobile MLX ceiling (MLXMemoryBudget, 4 GB) only
  engages MLX back-pressure before the kernel's limit if that limit sits above it.
  Entitlement-only — no developer-portal capability, automatic signing carries it.

  Signed: Kev + claude-fable-5.1, 2026-09-02, Confidence 0.8 (the entitlement is
  Apple's documented lever for exactly this; the 4 GB ceiling vs the real per-device
  jetsam budget is still the verify-owed measurement — os_proc_available_memory()
  on hardware). Prior: none (new file).
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
